# Build context rules for railway/Dockerfile.docs (the Docusaurus docs site).
#
# Why a separate file: the repo-root .dockerignore is tuned for the AGENT image,
# which does not need the website at all. It excludes `website/`, `*.md`, and
# `tests/`. Docker only honours ONE .dockerignore per build context, named after
# the Dockerfile — so building `railway/Dockerfile.docs` uses THIS file and
# ignores the root one entirely. That removes any chance of the two rule sets
# interacting, which is what silently stripped website/src/data/ and broke the
# build with "Can't resolve '@site/src/data/userStories.json'".

# Version control and CI config
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
venv
env

# Build artefacts
build
**/build
dist
**/dist
.docusaurus
**/.docusaurus
.cache
**/.cache

# Python bytecode
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# Secrets — never ship these into an image layer
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime data
/data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db

# Local agent state that has no business in a docs image
log.txt
*.log
